Subject: [PATCH] exynos990: stop the mark text from overwriting the stage bytes

sweet_early_mark() appends text at the start of the mark page and, since
0139, writes one byte per stage at +0x800.  The text cap was the whole
page (4096), so after about forty marks the text ran over the stage bytes
and erased marks that had just been written - a silent instrument failure
that looks exactly like a kernel that stopped earlier than it did.

Cap the text at 0x800 and leave the stage area alone.

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/sweet_early.c b/osfmk/arm64/sweet_early.c
--- a/osfmk/arm64/sweet_early.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/sweet_early.c
@@ -66,3 +66,3 @@
 #define SWEET_MARK_BASE ((uintptr_t)&intstack_low_guard)
-#define SWEET_MARK_CAP  4096u
+#define SWEET_MARK_CAP  0x800u	/* text stops before the stage bytes */
 
